Failover
   7. fence-a  site a (waits for the site if unreachable)
      fence Cluster pg-a: declare pg-b primary, so it never runs as primary again
        patch Cluster db/pg-a (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-b","promotionToken":null}}}
   8. pooler-a  site a (waits for the site if unreachable)
      set Pooler pg-a-pooler-rw to 0 instances
        patch Pooler db/pg-a-pooler-rw (merge): {"spec":{"instances":0}}
   9. wait-pooler-a  site a (waits for the site if unreachable)
      wait until the Pooler pg-a-pooler-rw runs no pod
        wait up to 10m0s on Deployment db/pg-a-pooler-rw until:
          {.status.replicas} is empty
  10. promote-b  site b
      promote Cluster pg-b without a token
        patch Cluster db/pg-b (merge): {"spec":{"replica":{"primary":"pg-b","promotionToken":null}}}
  11. wait-promoted-b  site b
      wait until Cluster pg-b runs a healthy primary
        wait up to 10m0s on Cluster db/pg-b until:
          {.status.instancesReportedState.*.isPrimary} Contains "true"
          {.status.phase} Equals "Cluster in healthy state"
  12. pooler-b  site b
